    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm looking for some advice on pallet stacking for our new high-density racking system in Rotterdam. We're dealing with some pretty heavy industrial loads. What's the best way to handle the center of gravity and interlocking patterns to make sure the stacks stays stable?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For high-density racking systems, especially in a location like Rotterdam with heavy loads, it's crucial to maintain a low center of gravity to ensure stability. Place the heavier items at the bottom, and lighter ones above, ensuring short and sturdy pallet feet are used to enhance support and avoid lean between stacks. Regarding interlocking, use standardized pallet designs that secure well amongst each other, possibly even employing interlocking bands or furniture fixings tailored for your racking system. Regular loading pattern inspections are also advised to prevent uneven weight distribution.",
